From: OPX <dev@opx.local>
Subject: [PATCH] USB: hub: accept low-speed device with maxpacket=64 (issue #85)

When the host USB stack (e.g. Xiaomi/MIUI) misreports a full-speed
device as low-speed, the guest kernel rejects it because low-speed
devices must have ep0 maxpacket=8, not 64.

This patch adds a fallback: if a low-speed device reports maxpacket=64,
accept it and treat the device as full-speed instead of rejecting it.

This is a safety net for when the QEMU host-libusb quirk is unavailable.

--- a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
@@ in hub_port_init(), before the "Invalid ep0 maxpacket" check:
-            dev_err(&udev->dev, "Invalid ep0 maxpacket: %d\n",
-                    usb_endpoint_maxp(&udev->ep0.desc));
-            goto err;
+            /* Xiaomi/MIUI host stack bug: full-speed devices misreported
+             * as low-speed. Accept maxpacket=64 and treat as full-speed.
+             * (issue #85 backup — primary fix is in QEMU host-libusb.c)
+             */
+            if (udev->speed == USB_SPEED_LOW &&
+                usb_endpoint_maxp(&udev->ep0.desc) == 64) {
+                dev_dbg(&udev->dev,
+                    "low-speed device with maxpacket=64, "
+                    "accepting as full-speed (host stack bug)\n");
+                udev->speed = USB_SPEED_FULL;
+            } else {
+                dev_err(&udev->dev, "Invalid ep0 maxpacket: %d\n",
+                        usb_endpoint_maxp(&udev->ep0.desc));
+                goto err;
+            }
